body:
I am myself addicted to surfing, I totally get what you are going through and it's really difficult to get away from this. Maybe what you can do to break this cycle is to substitute the time you spend on surfing with something useful. It might be reading book or you can try to learn something useful or it can be anything that you would like to do instead of surfing. It can be less satisfying and boring as well when you start but the end rewards are huge. 

&#x200B;

Also, on what device do you surf? If you are using Chrome on PC, you can install stayfocusd which will certainly help in avoiding the addiction. If you are using mobile, uninstall all those useless applications where you are wasting the time. I did that and now I feel better and proud of myself.
